---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const online = site.pricing.onlinePaymentsEnabled;
---
<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and stores your personal information.`}
>
  <p>
    This page explains what {site.legal.entityName} does with your personal information when you use this
    website or become a member. It is written to describe what actually happens, not to cover every
    imaginable case.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legal.entityName}, running yoga studios in Anjar and Adipur, Kutch, Gujarat, India. Our
    registered address and phone number are at the bottom of every page of this website.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
  <p>When you send the enquiry form on this website:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name and mobile number, so we can reply.</li>
    <li>Your email address, studio preference and message, if you fill them in.</li>
    <li>
      The internet address (IP address) your message came from. This is used only to stop one person
      or machine flooding the form, and for nothing else.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>When you become a member:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, mobile number and email address.</li>
    <li>Which plan you bought, when it starts and when it ends, and how you paid.</li>
    <li>A reference number for the payment, so a payment can be matched to your membership.</li>
    <li>When we sent you a renewal reminder, so you do not get the same message twice.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not collect anything else. There is no advertising, no tracking across other websites, and
    no analytics on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Card and bank details</h2>
  <p>
    We never see or store your card number, UPI PIN, or bank login. {online
      ? 'Online payments are handled entirely by Razorpay, who are regulated for this purpose. We receive only a reference number and the amount.'
      : 'Online card payment is not switched on yet. When it is, payments will be handled entirely by Razorpay, who are regulated for this purpose, and we will receive only a reference number and the amount.'}
    If you pay by UPI directly, the money moves between your app and our bank, and we see only what
    your app shows us.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else can see your information</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your information and we do not share it for marketing. It reaches these companies
    only because they run parts of this service for us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> stores the member and enquiry records. Our data is held in Mumbai, India.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> serves this website and keeps short-lived server logs.</li>
    <li><strong>Razorpay</strong> processes online payments, when that is switched on.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> sends the sign-in and notification emails, when that is switched on.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google</strong> receives your IP address when your browser loads the fonts and the
      embedded maps on this site. This happens on almost every website and we do not control it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We will also hand over information if the law requires it, for example a valid order from a court
    or the police.
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    If you sign in to see your membership, your browser keeps a sign-in token so you do not have to
    sign in again on every page, along with your first name so the menu can greet you. Both stay on
    your own device and are removed when you sign out. There are no advertising cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Enquiries: until we have dealt with them, and then for up to a year in case you come back.</li>
    <li>
      Membership and payment records: while you are a member, and afterwards for as long as tax and
      accounting rules require.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you can ask us to show you what we hold
    about you, correct anything wrong, or delete it. Write to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will reply within thirty days. We may
    need to keep payment records even after a deletion request, because tax rules require it.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not happy with our answer, you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Students under eighteen are welcome in class, but the membership and this website should be set
    up by a parent or guardian, who is the person we deal with.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it. Members will be told
    about anything significant.
  </p>
</Legal>
